%N A398966 Number of regions of an n question Venn diagram that can be filled by multisets of positive integers. Question k of n: Do one or more elements of the multiset sum to k?
%C A398966 The total number of regions in the n-th Venn diagram is given by A000079(n). a(6) records that 48 out of the 64 regions can be filled.
%C A398966 The fraction of regions that are filled asymptotically approaches zero.
%C A398966 This is a wonderful Venn puzzle for young students to practice addition.
%F A398966 a(n) <= 2*a(n-1). - _David A. Corneth_, Aug 23 2026
%e A398966 a(3) = 2^3 = 8 because every region of the 3 question Venn diagram can be filled:
%e A398966 The multiset {} fulfills no questions.
%e A398966 The multiset {1} fulfills question 1.
%e A398966 The multiset {2} fulfills question 2.
%e A398966 The multiset {3} fulfills question 3.
%e A398966 The multiset {1,1} fulfills questions 1,2.
%e A398966 The multiset {1,3} fulfills questions 1,3.
%e A398966 The multiset {2,3} fulfills questions 2,3.
%e A398966 The multiset {1,2} fulfills questions 1,2,3.
%e A398966 The multisets are not necessarily unique. For example, {1,1,1} also fulfills questions 1,2,3.
%e A398966 a(4) = 2^4 - 1 = 15 because it is possible to find multisets of positive integers that fill every region of the 4 question Venn diagram with one exception. In particular there is no multiset that fulfills questions 1,3 without also fulfilling either question 2 or 4. For example {1,3} fulfills questions 1,3,4 and {1,2} fulfills questions 1,2,3.
%e A398966 We may represent "set that satisfies questions 1,3, but not 2,4" as 1010 where the first 1 denotes question 1 satisfied and the second 0 denotes questions 2 not satisfied. As 1010 has no such set we don't have to check any question results starting with 1010. - _David A. Corneth_, Aug 23 2026
%o A398966 (PARI) a(n) = local(m=(2<<n)-1, v=[], f(s)=for(i=1, n, my(t=bitor(s, bitand(m, s<<i))); if(!setsearch(v, t), v=setunion(v, [t]); self()(t)))); f(1); 1+#v; \\ _Jinyuan Wang_, Aug 23 2026
%Y A398966 Cf. A000079.
